# Direction & look & reveal

## Scope: chapter vs video

- **Chapter 1 follows video look** — changing Background/Backdrop on a chapter saves **for that chapter**; “All chapters” applies globally. UI must state scope plainly (user asked for better copy than legacy wall of text).
- **Look & reveal** on chapter/caption cards: WebGL/plate backgrounds apply here too — not only full HTML plates.
- Renderer must respect **per-chapter** vs **global** background when user picks “apply to all” for look changes.

## Live preview in direction

- Fields should **live-update** stage (optimistic paint where legacy did) — scrubbers and motion fields wired to engine, not static placeholders.
- Avoid **full panel remount** when one subfield changes (lists reloading) — update narrow store slices / bridge callbacks.

## Inspector coherence

- Copy edit, magnifier, scaling, motion panels share **panel chrome** (radius, toolbar, collapsible sections, dividers).
- Hide internal debug strings (e.g. `clear · enter 860ms · stagger…`) from author-facing UI.

## Plate templates & backgrounds

- Template tiles: **static still** of background + label (no heavy animation in picker).
- Branded colors must flow into WebGL fields — templates agent-facing in `kit/templates/`.

## Critic / story

- **Run critic** → agent with critic skill, report output — not a no-op button.
- Story purpose radios: saving must use **`withPurpose`** ordering so purpose isn’t overwritten when rebuilding config (`narrative.mjs`).

## QC → Review → Feedback

- QC warnings button opens **Review**; selectable findings; **Apply selected / Apply all** via AI in Feedback — triage then execute (user chose this journey).
